cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ESTIF: Emergent Spacetime from Inward Flow — Geometric Tilt Model for Gravity, Dark Energy, and Dark Matter"
abstract: >-
  ESTIF v6.3 ("The Split") derives gravity from a single geometric claim: 3D
  space is a flat hypersurface carried through a 4D bulk, with everything moving
  through the bulk at the speed of light.

  HEADLINE MILESTONE (v6.3): The gravitational field equation is now DERIVED
  rather than matched to the Schwarzschild solution. Starting only from the flow
  axioms — flat 3-slices, universal speed c, and "empty space is not a source" —
  the Gauss-Codazzi (ADM) engine forces rho_eff = m'(r)/(4 pi r^2), i.e. mass
  continuity / Poisson's equation in integrated form. Consequences (engine-
  verified): vacuum gives v^2 = 2GM/r uniquely and exact Schwarzschild; a
  uniform-density source returns rho0 exactly. The former "Poisson postulate" is
  now a theorem for vacuum, Newton, and Schwarzschild. Lorentzian signature and
  special-relativistic kinematics also emerge from a Euclidean bulk plus the
  universal speed-c constraint. PRECISION: what the axioms establish is that they
  uniquely select the constraint (energy) sector of General Relativity in
  Painleve-Gullstrand gauge, without matching to the Schwarzschild solution. The
  gravitational coupling (geometric constraint scalar to 8*pi*G times energy
  density) is adopted from Einstein-Hilbert, not derived from below. Scripts:
  estif_task4_field_equation.py, estif_flow_signature_dynamics.py,
  estif_converse_flow_law.py, estif_tmunu_gauss_codazzi.py.

  PROJECT SPLIT (v6.3): the project forks into Path One (ESTIF-Core, clean) and
  Path Two (ESTIF-Extended, hard). Path One: gravity on the derived field
  equation; cosmology as a frozen cosmic eddy = cosmological constant, which ties
  LCDM on DESI DR2 (chi^2/N = 1.92). Path Two: derive a small thawing correction
  to w = -1 from the full rotating-shear/vorticity stress tensor.

  COSMOLOGY REFRAME (v6.3): the Omega_tilt(z) sector's DESI DR2 failure was traced
  to circularity (x(z) used H_LCDM as its own ruler). A self-consistent
  fixed-point solve (estif_task5_desi_selfconsistent.py) drops chi^2/N from 10.8
  to 3.35, but the frozen-eddy limit (w = -1) ties LCDM at 1.92 and beats the
  tilt formula's 3.35. Attempts to derive the eddy equation of state
  (estif_task6_eddy_eos.py) show the two natural reductions fail badly (stiff
  spin chi^2/N = 3232; expansion tracker 754), so the Omega_tilt apparatus is
  retired from the cosmology claim; its local strong-field use is unaffected.

  Prior gravity results carried forward and now on a derived foundation:
  MOND a0 = H0*c*x0/sqrt(3) = 1.179e-10 m/s^2 (1.72% from empirical), validated
  against 87 quality-1 SPARC galaxies (RMS 15.6%); a0 redshift constancy proved
  (H(z) cancels in the comoving frame); parameter independence across 3,600
  H0/Omega_m combinations. Strong-field local tilt: EHT M87* shadow 0.00 sigma,
  Planck Lambda ratio 1.0000, LISA GW delay 491 us at S/N 49.2 sigma; GR time
  dilation is the special case at n=1/2 (x=0.272). CAVEAT: because the derived
  ESTIF vacuum is exactly Schwarzschild, any predicted DEVIATION from GR in
  black-hole shadows or in vacuum gravitational-wave propagation must be sourced
  by the non-vacuum eddy background, a sector not yet derived. The observations
  above are consistent with ESTIF; the deviation-from-GR figures are conditional
  on that open derivation. The Planck Lambda entry is a calibration match, not a
  vacuum deviation, and is unaffected.

  Dark matter analytical results: Omega_m = x0 = R_H/r_universe to 0.12%,
  Omega_dm = x0 - Omega_b to 0.10%. These are CONSISTENCY RELATIONS, not
  Omega_m-independent predictions: r_universe is here the LCDM particle horizon,
  an integral that itself depends on Omega_m. The numerical agreement stands; an
  independent prediction requires deriving r_universe from the flow framework.
  N-body simulation needed for halo structure.

  OMEGA_M BOOTSTRAP (v6.3.2, CONDITIONAL): adopting principle P (Omega_m = R_H/r_p)
  closes the C2 circularity into Omega_m * I(Omega_m) = 1, which has a unique root:
  0.3043 with zero measured inputs, 0.31408 with radiation (inputs T_CMB, N_eff, h)
  -- 0.96% from Planck, 0.53 sigma inside its error bar. It back-predicts
  r_universe = 4.353e26 m (-1.07%). Closure: a0 = 1.1920e-10 m/s^2 (MOND agreement
  1.72% -> 0.66%); DESI DR2 chi^2/N = 1.618 (fixed-ruler). Input ledger: measured =
  {H0, T_CMB, N_eff}; computed = {Omega_m, Omega_Lambda, x0, r_universe, a0}.
  Identity: P is equivalent to mean matter pull at the horizon = c*H0/2, the same
  c*H0 that sets a0. CONDITIONAL: P is not derived from the flow axioms (open); a
  comparison with Gaztanaga's causal-universe scale (~0.3176 H0) is a prerequisite
  for any novelty claim. Scripts: estif_omega_bootstrap.py, estif_bootstrap_closure.py.

  A fidelity audit (estif_fidelity_audit.py) found that the axioms of universal
  speed c (A2) and "empty space is not a source" (A3) lived only in the derivation
  scripts, and that the concept document ran a competing shrinking-ruler
  narrative. Both were corrected in the v6.3 concept rewrite: A1-A3 are now stated
  explicitly in ESTIF_CONCEPT.md, the shrinking-ruler picture is retired in favour
  of the flat-slice flow (Painleve-Gullstrand) picture, and v_flow = c*x0 is
  relabelled as the sideways component of a total-c motion rather than the full
  flow speed.

